<p>Hello pineappleseed!</p>
<p>Happy to have you here! Trevor has some amazing works, and they do certainly give off those surreal horror vibes that a lot of earlier skips tend to follow. Regardless of that though, there's no rush to contribute to the site, so do take things at your own pace! Take all the time you need to explore and learn how the site works. The best way to learn about the site and how things work is really just to read and explore the content that's here. I'll provide you with both a reading list that'll take you all over the site as well as a writing guide since you do have an eventual interest in creating a skip. But again, take things at your own pace, and feel free to reach out if you have any further questions!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Reading&nbsp;list.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Hope&nbsp;this&nbsp;helps!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Maybe you've already seen these before, maybe you haven't, but hopefully something here is of use to you. Of course, if you have any questions, feel free to reach out!</p>
<p>The newest, freshest material can be found on the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/most-recently-created">Most Recently Created</a> page. If that updates a little too frequently for you though and you want more of a look at what remains popular, you can also try the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/top-rated-pages-this-month">Top Rated New Pages</a>.</p>
<p>If you want to see what other folks in the community like, there's the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/user-curated-lists">User-Curated Lists</a>. Here you can find things the community has put together and deemed a good read. Or maybe you want to give some underrated articles some love? Try out the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/young-and-under-30">Underread and Underrated</a> page.</p>
<p>Enjoy large hubs and working your way through them? Some cool hubs include the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for things that cover the Site itself, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/news">Site News Hub</a> for updates on all sorts of monthly Site content, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/canon-hub">Canon Hub</a> for all the various canons, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/goi-formats">GoI Format Hub</a> for all your GoI needs, and <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/foundation-tales">Tales Hub</a> for your favorite tales.</p>
<p>Finally, if you find an author you love from any of this and want to see more from them, you can find them in the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/members-pages">Authors' Pages</a> section. If they're not on that list, try the statistic site, <a href="http://scpper.com">scpper.com</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Writer's&nbsp;info</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Hope&nbsp;this&nbsp;helps!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Maybe you've already seen these before, maybe you haven't, but hopefully something here is of use to you. Of course, if you have any questions, feel free to reach out!</p>
<p>First off, there are some required readings for all site authors. Consider giving them a read, as well as all the other helpful guides on this <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/guide-hub">Guide Hub.</a> The more familiar you are with the processes that take place on the Site, the better your chances of success are!</p>
<p>Now that that's done - Got an idea? Or maybe a few? You can create a <a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/">Sandbox</a> page to store all your ideas and drafts in an orderly fashion.</p>
<p>Okay, but maybe you're not sure if your concept is ready to be fleshed out, or perhaps it just needs some heavy refinement. If that's the case, you can run things by the community in the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-and-brainstorming">Ideas and Brainstorming</a> forum.</p>
<p>Once you believe you have a solid draft, you can go ahead and make a thread in the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/c-50864/help:drafts-and-critiques">Drafts and Critiques</a> forum. Keep in mind though you should check the stickied posts first on how best to use each of the forums.</p>
<p>Best of luck writing!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

